  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want the legacy reader bars: one \"⋯\" at the top right, page arrows at the bottom left, the next-page arrow highlighted when I reach the end of a page, and a highlighted refresh button only at the end of the last page, so that the next useful action is always under my thumb.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 08, 12, 13 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Observed (2026-11-11)\n| | Legacy @ `87fe0d1c` | SwiftHFR @ `9e93c3eb` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Top bar | Title + \"page / last\" subtitle, **one \"⋯\"** | Larger title, **refresh + \"⋯\"** |\n| Bottom bar | ‹ › leading, reply \"+\" trailing | ‹ › leading, **\"1 / 1 126\" page button** centre, no \"+\" |\n| End of a page that is not the last | › becomes prominent (`glassProminent`) | No change |\n| End of the last page | Prominent **refresh** button appears; the only refresh in the reader | No button; refresh stays in the top bar |\n\nLegacy: `shouldPromoteBottomNextPageButton` and `shouldShowBottomRefreshButton`, `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:4972-4978`; buttons `topicBottomBarButtonStyle(isProminent:)` (commit `cf93fbd1`).\n\n### Scope\n- Top: remove the refresh button; one \"⋯\". Title with the \"page / last\" subtitle (to confirm by the operator).\n- Bottom: remove the page button (operator: \"ça c'est non\"); page choice stays in \"⋯\" and the title. Keep SwiftHFR's ‹ › style (operator).\n- End-of-page states as legacy, driven by \"scrolled to the bottom\" and \"last page or not\".\n- The reply \"+\" is #654.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At the bottom of page N < last: › is prominent; scrolling up turns it back.\n- [ ] At the bottom of the last page: a prominent refresh appears; it reloads and keeps the position.\n- [ ] No refresh in the top bar; no page button in the bottom bar.\n\nRelated: #654 (reply \"+\"), #641 (insets), GAP-060.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
